    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d848">

                <pb facs="1196" n="1176" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg1176"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/11–1750</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Executive Secretary of the National
                        Security Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the National Security Council Senior Staff </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-11-17">November 17,
                        1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: U.S. Courses of Action with Respect to Korea</p>
                <table>
                    <row>
                        <cell rendition="#top">References:</cell>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>. NSC 81/2<anchor n="1" xml:id="d848-f1"/>
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                        <cell/>
                        <cell rendition="#hanging-indent">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>. Record of Meeting of the Senior NSC
                            Staff, November 16, 1950, paragraph 2.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d848-f2"/>
                        </cell>
                    </row>
                </table>
                <p>The enclosed draft interim report on the subject, submitted by the Senior Defense
                        member<anchor n="3" xml:id="d848-f3"/> in accordance with the agreement at
                    the Senior Staff meeting on November 16, is transmitted herewith for
                    consideration by the Senior Staff at its meeting on Monday, November 20, at 2:30
                    p. m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay,
                            Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d848-a1.xml" xpointer="d848-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
